  A MERGE RULE IS DERIVABLE only if the WITHIN-word gaps and the
  BETWEEN-word gaps separate. The between-word gap is bounded below by the
  trial's silent tail, so mass well above that is the real boundary and
  mass well below it is chatter to be merged across. If ON/word is near 1
  the gate already finds the word and only shatters it, which is the case a
  merge rule fixes; if it is well under 1 the gate is also MISSING the
  word and merging alone cannot recover it.

